#9900
Statues On The Crypt~
   You are standing atop the crypt, overlooking the mists and cold
vapours of the corrupted cemetary.  From here you can see out across the
cemetary to view the mindless wanderings of the various undead that lumber
around the grasses and tombs below you, stopping only to gnaw on a bone
or rip into a half-buried casket.
   Two statues stand here; the first of which is that of an elvish thief,
possibly the matron of the family to whom the crypt belongs.  The smaller
one is that of a sandstone cat, standing on its back paws to claw at an
unseen fly.
   Sturdy vines, some as large as tree trunks, descend the top of the
tomb to the east and west, allowing you to smoothly climb down without
having to leap.  To the north, the cemetary wall rises high above
the back of the tomb.
~
