#9952
Northern Cemetary Wall~
   You are standing below the northern wall of the cemetary, just
east of a white marble crypt.  Ivy and vines climb from the long-
neglected ground to envelop the crypt in their pallid grasp.
   Several tombstones lie flat here on the grass, crushing the life
from the plants and reeds beneath them and providing solid depressions
from which you can avoid the tall, stiff grasses that brush against
your legs.
   The cemetary comtinues to the east and south.
