#9987
A Warrior's Last Battle~
   You are standing in a bone-strewn corridor.  The corpse of a recently
dead warrior lies here; the decay on his face telling that he could have
been dead no more than a year.
   His armour, had we worn any, must have been stripped at the time of
his demise.  The stench of death seems to have long since left the corpse,
leaving only the bloated husk of a corpse resting on a shattered bastard
sword.
   The hall continues to the north and south.
~
